Patch summary:
On virtio-gpu, which takes only linear frame buffers, add a frame buffer
without the DRM format modifier the gralloc reports for the buffer. In the
venus and honeykrisp GPU modes the host allocates SurfaceFlinger's client
target as a tiled image and scans it out with that layout itself (crosvm's
PATCH.crosvm-scanout-blob-modifier.patch), while the guest's Vulkan driver
renders into it with the modifier; the composer refused the buffer ("No
ADDFB2 with modifier support") and showed nothing.

diff --git a/drm/DrmFbImporter.cpp b/drm/DrmFbImporter.cpp
index fe80891..12b105b 100644
--- a/drm/DrmFbImporter.cpp
+++ b/drm/DrmFbImporter.cpp
@@ -65,6 +65,14 @@ auto DrmFbIdHandle::CreateInstance(BufferInfo *bo, GemHandle first_gem_handle,
   auto has_modifiers = bo->modifiers[0] != DRM_FORMAT_MOD_NONE &&
                        bo->modifiers[0] != DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID;
 
+  /* Ika: virtio-gpu takes only linear frame buffers, but the host keeps the
+   * buffer in the layout it gave it (a tiled one in Venus and Honeykrisp
+   * modes) and opens a scanout with that layout itself. */
+  if (!drm.HasAddFb2ModifiersSupport() && has_modifiers &&
+      drm.GetName() == "virtio_gpu") {
+    has_modifiers = false;
+  }
+
   if (!drm.HasAddFb2ModifiersSupport() && has_modifiers) {
     ALOGE("No ADDFB2 with modifier support. Can't import modifier %" PRIu64,
           bo->modifiers[0]);
